{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1791357758062,"sessionID":"ses_eeac95740ffejVNLcFbklV5Ztd","part":{"id":"prt_1153e2a65001nuOHS6m3dxcVYJ","messageID":"msg_1153e1d95001eInb4mTGsGZ0by","sessionID":"ses_eeac95740ffejVNLcFbklV5Ztd","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791357764675,"sessionID":"ses_eeac95740ffejVNLcFbklV5Ztd","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"tyNS92J4OlMqU4nv","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cat << 'EOF' > data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_1/hypothesis.md\nListeners interpret the speaker as describing an object chosen according to their evaluative attitude, where desirability increases with feature complexity. When a speaker describes their favorite object, listeners infer that they favor referents with more features, whereas when describing their least favorite object, they favor referents with fewer features. Listeners invert this value-conditioned speaker upon hearing an utterance, and default to the speaker's evaluative preference when no informative word is given.\nEOF\n\ncat << 'EOF' > data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_1/model_name.txt\nvalence_evaluative_listener\nEOF\n\ncat << 'EOF' > data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_1/candidate.py\n\"\"\"Evaluative listener reasoning about an affective, value-conditioned speaker.\n\nThe listener models a speaker who communicates about a referent chosen\naccording to their evaluative attitude (valence): a speaker describing their\nfavorite object favors referents with more features, while a speaker\ndescribing their least favorite object favors referents with fewer features.\nOn neutral trials, referent preference is uniform. The listener inverts this\nvalue-conditioned speaker upon hearing an utterance, and chooses by the\nevaluative preference when no informative word is given. A lapse parameter\nmixes in uniform guessing.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport numpyro.distributions as dist\nfrom memo import memo\n\nfrom src.rsa.memo_kit import EPS, at, softmax_prior, vec, with_lapse\n\nPARAMS = {\n    \"alpha\": dist.LogNormal(0.0, 1.0),\n    \"beta_valence\": dist.Normal(0.0, 2.0),\n    \"lapse\": dist.Beta(1.0, 9.0),\n}\n\n\n@memo\ndef L0[u: UTT, r: OBJ](lex: ...):\n    listener: knows(u)\n    listener: chooses(r in OBJ, wpp=at(lex, u, r))\n    return Pr[listener.r == r]\n\n\n@memo\ndef L1[u: UTT, r: OBJ](alpha, lex: ..., eval_prior: ...):\n    listener: thinks[\n        speaker: given(r in OBJ, wpp=vec(eval_prior, r)),\n        speaker: chooses(u in UTT, wpp=at(lex, u, r) * exp(alpha * log(L0[u, r](lex) + {EPS}))),\n    ]\n    listener: observes [speaker.u] is u\n    listener: chooses(r in OBJ, wpp=Pr[speaker.r == r])\n    return Pr[listener.r == r]\n\n\ndef choice_probs(params, ctx):\n    eval_prior = softmax_prior(params[\"beta_valence\"] * ctx.valence * ctx.feature_count)\n    heard = L1(params[\"alpha\"], ctx.lex, eval_prior)[ctx.utterance]\n    return with_lapse(jnp.where(ctx.is_prior > 0, eval_prior, heard), params[\"lapse\"])\nEOF"},"output":"(no output)","metadata":{"output":"(no output)","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cat << 'EOF' > data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_1/hypothesis.md\nListeners interpret the speaker as describing an object chosen according to their evaluative attitude, where desirability increases with feature complexity. When a speaker describes their favorite object, listeners infer that they favor referents with more features, whereas when describing their least favorite object, they favor referents with fewer features. Listeners invert this value-conditioned speaker upon hearing an utterance, and default to the speaker's evaluative preference when no informative word is given.\nEOF\n\ncat << 'EOF' > data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_1/model_name.txt\nvalence_evaluative_listener\nEOF\n\ncat << 'EOF' > data/rsa/loop_smoke2_repair/round_1/candidate_1/candidate.py\n\"\"\"Evaluative listener reasoning about an affective, value-conditioned speaker.\n\nThe listener models a speaker who communicates about a referent chosen\naccording to their evaluative attitude (valence): a speaker describing their\nfavorite object favors referents with more features, while a speaker\ndescribing their least favorite object favors referents with fewer features.\nOn neutral trials, referent preference is uniform. The listener inverts this\nvalue-conditioned speaker upon hearing an utterance, and chooses by the\nevaluative preference when no informative word is given. A lapse parameter\nmixes in uniform guessing.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport numpyro.distributions as dist\nfrom memo import memo\n\nfrom src.rsa.memo_kit import EPS, at, softmax_prior, vec, with_lapse\n\nPARAMS = {\n    \"alpha\": dist.LogNormal(0.0, 1.0),\n    \"beta_valence\": dist.Normal(0.0, 2.0),\n    \"lapse\": dist.Beta(1.0, 9.0),\n}\n\n\n@memo\ndef L0[u: UTT, r: OBJ](lex: ...):\n    listener: knows(u)\n    listener: chooses(r in OBJ, wpp=at(lex, u, r))\n    return Pr[listener.r == r]\n\n\n@memo\ndef L1[u: UTT, r: OBJ](alpha, lex: ..., eval_prior: ...):\n    listener: thinks[\n        speaker: given(r in OBJ, wpp=vec(eval_prior, r)),\n        speaker: chooses(u in UTT, wpp=at(lex, u, r) * exp(alpha * log(L0[u, r](lex) + {EPS}))),\n    ]\n    listener: observes [speaker.u] is u\n    listener: chooses(r in OBJ, wpp=Pr[speaker.r == r])\n    return Pr[listener.r == r]\n\n\ndef choice_probs(params, ctx):\n    eval_prior = softmax_prior(params[\"beta_valence\"] * ctx.valence * ctx.feature_count)\n    heard = L1(params[\"alpha\"], ctx.lex, eval_prior)[ctx.utterance]\n    return with_lapse(jnp.where(ctx.is_prior > 0, eval_prior, heard), params[\"lapse\"])\nEOF","time":{"start":1791357764595,"end":1791357764635}},"metadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}},"id":"prt_1153e43e1001eBuXVu3Bn3oEEG","sessionID":"ses_eeac95740ffejVNLcFbklV5Ztd","messageID":"msg_1153e1d95001eInb4mTGsGZ0by"}}
